234 0 obj
<< /A 714 0 R /ActualText (Flowchart illustrating the advisor recommendation algorithm. University provides teacher data, including course, research, and publicationrecords. This data is preprocessed into truncated or padded sentences. Simultaneously, students input short-text queries, and the advisor recommendation algorithm matches suitable teachers in the teacher database based on the pooling and matching criteria, and generates a list of recommended advisors. Student feedback closes the loop to enhance recommendation quality.\r\n) /Alt (Flowchart illustrating the advisor recommendation algorithm. University provides teacher data, including course, research, and publicationrecords. This data is preprocessed into truncated or padded sentences. Simultaneously, students input short-text queries, and the advisor recommendation algorithm matches suitable teachers in the teacher database based on the pooling and matching criteria, and generates a list of recommended advisors. Student feedback closes the loop to enhance recommendation quality.\r\n) /K 0 /P 93 0 R /Pg 223 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
235 0 obj
<< /A 715 0 R /ActualText (Flowchart illustrating the network architecture of AVRD model. It consists of two parts: BERT and SimCSE. During the training process, sentences are fed into the BERT to generate sentence embedding vectors. Subsequently, for each vector in the sampled batch extracted from the sentence embedding set, the vector is paired with itself to form a positive instance and with other vectors to form negative instances, followed by the generation of a corresponding batch-wise instance set. The BERT network is fine-tuned using the unsupervised SimCSE approach, aiming to enhance the representational capacity of the sentence embeddings.\r\n) /Alt (Flowchart illustrating the network architecture of AVRD model. It consists of two parts: BERT and SimCSE. During the training process, sentences are fed into the BERT to generate sentence embedding vectors. Subsequently, for each vector in the sampled batch extracted from the sentence embedding set, the vector is paired with itself to form a positive instance and with other vectors to form negative instances, followed by the generation of a corresponding batch-wise instance set. The BERT network is fine-tuned using the unsupervised SimCSE approach, aiming to enhance the representational capacity of the sentence embeddings.\r\n) /K 0 /P 93 0 R /Pg 224 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
236 0 obj
<< /A 716 0 R /ActualText (Charts illustrating the data distributions before and after questionnaire processing. The bar charts show the respondent counts by college before and after data cleaning. The doughnut charts display the grade and gender ratios, respectively, showing similar gender distributions. Despite a significant reduction in the total number of respondents after cleaning, these distributions remained stable.\r\n) /Alt (Charts illustrating the data distributions before and after questionnaire processing. The bar charts show the respondent counts by college before and after data cleaning. The doughnut charts display the grade and gender ratios, respectively, showing similar gender distributions. Despite a significant reduction in the total number of respondents after cleaning, these distributions remained stable.\r\n) /K 0 /P 93 0 R /Pg 227 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
237 0 obj
<< /A 717 0 R /ActualText (Scatter plot showing the visualization effect of research direction vectors. Colored dots in the scatter plot represent different schools \(1: blue, 2: orange, 9: yellow, 11: red, 12: green, 14: purple\). Schools 2, 9 and 11 exhibit high intraclass compactness, whereas the other three schools show obvious intra-class dispersion. School 1 has a subcategory that tends to cluster with School 9. School 12 shows slight overlap with Schools 2 and 9. School 14 also has a subcategory biased towards School 11.\r\n) /Alt (Scatter plot showing the visualization effect of research direction vectors. Colored dots in the scatter plot represent different schools \(1: blue, 2: orange, 9: yellow, 11: red, 12: green, 14: purple\). Schools 2, 9 and 11 exhibit high intraclass compactness, whereas the other three schools show obvious intra-class dispersion. School 1 has a subcategory that tends to cluster with School 9. School 12 shows slight overlap with Schools 2 and 9. School 14 also has a subcategory biased towards School 11.\r\n) /K 0 /P 93 0 R /Pg 230 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
238 0 obj
<< /A 718 0 R /ActualText (Scatter plot showing the visualization effect of course vectors. Colored dots in the scatter plot represent different schools \(1: blue, 2: orange, 9: yellow, 11: red, 12: green, 14: purple\). The course records of teachers across different schools exhibit clear inter-school distinctions, and the overlap phenomenon is reduced. \r\n) /Alt (Scatter plot showing the visualization effect of course vectors. Colored dots in the scatter plot represent different schools \(1: blue, 2: orange, 9: yellow, 11: red, 12: green, 14: purple\). The course records of teachers across different schools exhibit clear inter-school distinctions, and the overlap phenomenon is reduced. \r\n) /K 1 /P 93 0 R /Pg 230 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
239 0 obj
<< /A 719 0 R /ActualText (Scatter plot showing the visualization effect of paper publication vectors. Colored dots in the scatter plot represent different schools \(1: blue, 2: orange, 9: yellow, 11: red, 12: green, 14: purple\). There is a minor overlap between School 14 and School 11, as well as among Schools 12, 1, 2 and 9. The 6 schools can be categorized into two groups: School 11 and School 14 are located on the right, while Schools 1, 2, 9,and 12 are situated on the left. \r\n) /Alt (Scatter plot showing the visualization effect of paper publication vectors. Colored dots in the scatter plot represent different schools \(1: blue, 2: orange, 9: yellow, 11: red, 12: green, 14: purple\). There is a minor overlap between School 14 and School 11, as well as among Schools 12, 1, 2 and 9. The 6 schools can be categorized into two groups: School 11 and School 14 are located on the right, while Schools 1, 2, 9,and 12 are situated on the left. \r\n) /K 2 /P 93 0 R /Pg 230 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
