514 0 obj
<< /BS << /W 0 >> /F 4 /FT /Btn /Ff 65536 /MK << /BC [ 0 0 0 0 ] >> /P 224 0 R /Rect [ 85.199997 241.640963 510.396973 746.092959 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (Figure2) /TU (Flowchart illustrating the network architecture of AVRD model. It consists of two parts: BERT and SimCSE. During the training process, sentences are fed into the BERT to generate sentence embedding vectors. Subsequently, for each vector in the sampled batch extracted from the sentence embedding set, the vector is paired with itself to form a positive instance and with other vectors to form negative instances, followed by the generation of a corresponding batch-wise instance set. The BERT network is fine-tuned using the unsupervised SimCSE approach, aiming to enhance the representational capacity of the sentence embeddings.) /Type /Annot >>
