622 0 obj
<< /BS << /W 0 >> /F 4 /FT /Btn /Ff 65536 /MK << /BC [ 0 0 0 0 ] >> /P 230 0 R /Rect [ 56.723999 597.644992 283.523987 745.334994 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (Figure4) /TU (Scatter plot showing the visualization effect of research direction vectors. Colored dots in the scatter plot represent different schools \(1: blue, 2: orange, 9: yellow, 11: red, 12: green, 14: purple\). Schools 2, 9 and 11 exhibit high intraclass compactness, whereas the other three schools show obvious intra-class dispersion. School 1 has a subcategory that tends to cluster with School 9. School 12 shows slight overlap with Schools 2 and 9. School 14 also has a subcategory biased towards School 11.) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
623 0 obj
<< /BS << /W 0 >> /F 4 /FT /Btn /Ff 65536 /MK << /BC [ 0 0 0 0 ] >> /P 230 0 R /Rect [ 311.666992 597.644992 538.438965 745.221988 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (Figure5) /TU (Scatter plot showing the visualization effect of course vectors. Colored dots in the scatter plot represent different schools \(1: blue, 2: orange, 9: yellow, 11: red, 12: green, 14: purple\). The course records of teachers across different schools exhibit clear inter-school distinctions, and the overlap phenomenon is reduced.) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
624 0 obj
<< /BS << /W 0 >> /F 4 /FT /Btn /Ff 65536 /MK << /BC [ 0 0 0 0 ] >> /P 230 0 R /Rect [ 311.666992 383.34598 538.438965 530.968966 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (Figure6) /TU (Scatter plot showing the visualization effect of paper publication vectors. Colored dots in the scatter plot represent different schools \(1: blue, 2: orange, 9: yellow, 11: red, 12: green, 14: purple\). There is a minor overlap between School 14 and School 11, as well as among Schools 12, 1, 2 and 9. The 6 schools can be categorized into two groups: School 11 and School 14 are located on the right, while Schools 1, 2, 9,and 12 are situated on the left.) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
